WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
In 2021, the world used
its last leaded petrol.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.350
Bans had pushed it out.

3
00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.700
In 2008, British Columbia, in Canada,

4
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:14.380
tried a different tool: a tax on
every tonne of carbon dioxide.

5
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.160
And since 2005, firms across
the European Union have

6
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.790
bought and sold permits to pollute.

7
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.430
So should a government tax pollution,

8
00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.890
ban it, or let firms trade
the right to pollute?

9
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.970
In this mission, you'll set the tax
on a polluting factory yourself,

10
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.990
and watch what happens to output.

11
00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:36.690
Then you'll follow two firms
as they buy and sell permits,

12
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:39.660
and count what cleaning up really costs.

13
00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: find out
what each tool does well,

14
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.750
and where each one falls short.
